[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4033591704","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116916#issuecomment-4033591704","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116916","id":4033591704,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7wa7mY","user":{"login":"Shadows-of-Fire","id":3682588,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODI1ODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3682588?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire","html_url":"https://github.com/Shadows-of-Fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-10T18:34:41Z","updated_at":"2026-03-10T18:34:41Z","body":"What indicates this is JSDoc-based? This looks like [Javadoc-syntax Doxygen](https://www.doxygen.nl/manual/docblocks.html). As far as I'm aware JSDoc does not have a `@brief` tag. If this was JSDoc it would be `@summary`.\r\n\r\nI'm fine with the style, but it's important that we, you know, actually reflect the selected style in the MR text. Doxygen is more C++ focused so it would make more sense to be in-line with that (which it more or less already is) and update the MR text rather than bringing things back in-line with JSDoc (which is primarily for JavaScript).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTO